## Scope and Limitations

This environment focuses on integrating reusable Terraform modules into a single configuration within one Azure subscription.

It does not currently represent a complete production Azure landing zone or a complete three-tier application architecture.

The current scope also excludes:

- Remote Terraform state management.
- Application Gateway or Load Balancer integration.
- Public IP attachment to the VM.
- Managed identity configuration.
- Confirmed end-to-end application connectivity.

Additional services should be introduced only when required by a specific learning objective.

## Learning Objectives

- Compose reusable Terraform modules.
- Manage dependencies between Azure resources.
- Configure VNets, subnets, NSGs, and VNet peering.
- Deploy a Linux VM using SSH authentication.
- Integrate a reusable Public IP module.
- Review Terraform plans before making infrastructure changes.
- Apply consistent tagging and configuration practices.
- Understand the implications of local Terraform state and state-file protection.